    { cat: 'meta', icon: 'blur_on',             label: 'Ambiguity Detector',     text: 'Scan the following prompt for ambiguity. For every ambiguous word, phrase, or instruction, flag it and explain what different readers might interpret it to mean.\\n\\nPrompt to analyse:\\n[paste prompt here]\\n\\nAmbiguities found:\\n1. "[ambiguous phrase]" — could mean: [interpretation A] or [interpretation B]\\n2. "[ambiguous phrase]" — could mean: [interpretation A] or [interpretation B]\\n...\\n\\nHighest-risk ambiguity: [the one most likely to cause a wrong output]\\nClarified version: [prompt rewritten to remove all ambiguity]' },
    { cat: 'meta', icon: 'fork_right',          label: 'Inference Chain',        text: 'Map the reasoning chain from the input to the desired output for this prompt.\\n\\nPrompt: [paste prompt here]\\n\\nInference chain:\\nStep 1: [what the AI must first understand or establish]\\nStep 2: [what it must reason from that]\\nStep 3: [what it then needs to conclude]\\nStep 4: [how that conclusion maps to the output format]\\n\\nWeak links in the chain: [where the reasoning could break]\\nStrengthening additions: [what to add to the prompt to support each weak link]' },
    { cat: 'meta', icon: 'science',             label: 'Hypothesis Generator',   text: 'Generate [N] testable hypotheses about the following question or observation:\\n\\nQuestion/Observation: [paste here]\\n\\nFor each hypothesis:\\n- Statement: [clear, falsifiable claim]\\n- Prediction: [what would be true if this hypothesis is correct]\\n- Test: [how you would test or disprove it]\\n- Prior probability: [high / medium / low — your confidence before testing]\\n\\nRank the hypotheses from most to least likely. Lead with the one most worth testing first.' },
    { cat: 'meta', icon: 'quiz',                label: 'Probe Questions',        text: 'Generate [N] probing questions to help uncover the real problem behind the stated one.\\n\\nStated problem: [what the person said the problem is]\\n\\nProbe questions (go deeper with each one):\\n1. [surface clarification]\\n2. [challenge the framing]\\n3. [explore the root cause]\\n4. [uncover hidden assumptions]\\n5. [reveal what success would actually look like]\\n...\\n\\nMost revealing question: [the one that would most change the approach if answered]' },
    { cat: 'meta', icon: 'loop',                label: 'Self-Critique Loop',     text: 'Generate a response, critique it rigorously, then generate a final improved version.\\n\\nTask: [your task here]\\n\\nFirst attempt:\\n[generate response]\\n\\nSelf-critique:\\n- What is weakest about this response?\\n- What assumptions did I make that might be wrong?\\n- What important angle did I miss?\\n- What would a sceptical reader object to?\\n- How does this compare to the best possible response?\\n\\nFinal version (incorporating all critique):\\n[improved response]' },
    { cat: 'meta', icon: 'compress',            label: 'Prompt Minimizer',       text: 'Strip this prompt down to its essential minimum without losing capability.\\n\\nOriginal prompt:\\n[paste prompt here]\\n\\nMinimization process:\\n1. Remove all instructions the model will follow by default anyway\\n2. Remove all redundant restatements of the same rule\\n3. Compress verbose instructions into tighter phrasing\\n4. Remove examples if the task is simple enough without them\\n5. Test the minimal version to verify output quality is maintained\\n\\nMinimal version:\\n[stripped-down prompt]\\n\\nWhat was removed and why: [list with reasoning]' },
    { cat: 'meta', icon: 'search',              label: 'Assumption Finder',      text: 'Identify every assumption embedded in the following prompt or plan.\\n\\nContent to analyse:\\n[paste here]\\n\\nAssumptions found:\\n1. [assumption] — Confidence: [high/med/low] — Risk if wrong: [high/med/low]\\n2. [assumption] — Confidence: [high/med/low] — Risk if wrong: [high/med/low]\\n3. [assumption] — Confidence: [high/med/low] — Risk if wrong: [high/med/low]\\n...\\n\\nMost dangerous assumption: [the one that, if wrong, breaks the whole approach]\\nHow to validate it: [fastest way to test this assumption]' },
    { cat: 'meta', icon: 'preview',             label: 'Output Predictor',       text: 'Predict what output this prompt will produce before running it.\\n\\nPrompt to analyse:\\n[paste prompt here]\\n\\nPredicted output characteristics:\\n- Format: [what structure the output will have]\\n- Length: [estimated length]\\n- Tone: [predicted tone and register]\\n- Content: [main points it will likely cover]\\n- What it will miss: [gaps or blind spots]\\n- Risk of hallucination: [high / medium / low — and why]\\n\\nSurprise prediction: [the most unexpected thing this prompt might produce]' },
    { cat: 'meta', icon: 'tune',                label: 'Tone Calibrator',        text: 'Rewrite the following prompt to produce output with a specific tone.\\n\\nOriginal prompt:\\n[paste prompt here]\\n\\nTarget tone: [e.g. executive-formal / conversational-warm / technical-precise / persuasive-energetic]\\n\\nTone dimensions to adjust:\\n- Formality: [1=casual, 5=formal] Target: [N]\\n- Directness: [1=diplomatic, 5=blunt] Target: [N]\\n- Detail level: [1=summary, 5=exhaustive] Target: [N]\\n- Emotional warmth: [1=cold, 5=warm] Target: [N]\\n\\nCalibrated prompt:\\n[rewritten to produce target tone]' },
    { cat: 'meta', icon: 'groups',              label: 'Audience Adapter',       text: 'Rewrite this prompt to produce output appropriate for a different audience.\\n\\nOriginal prompt:\\n[paste prompt here]\\n\\nTarget audience: [describe them — role, expertise level, what they care about, what they already know]\\n\\nAdaptations to make:\\n1. Vocabulary: [technical → plain / plain → technical / specialist jargon → general]\\n2. Examples: [use examples relevant to their world]\\n3. Format: [what format this audience prefers — bullets / prose / tables]\\n4. Depth: [how much background do they need?]\\n5. CTA: [what should they do with this information?]\\n\\nAdapted prompt:\\n[rewritten version]' },
